 {"id":"uf-1787984497755-7ebw7o","shape":"uiFeedback_write","visibility":"public","received_at":"2026-08-29T06:21:37.758Z","pointer":{"type":"uiFeedback_write","id":"uf-1787984497755-7ebw7o","panel_id":"needs-human-lift-gate-confidence-term-passes-when-activity-drops","value":"I am providing missing information for this gap. Here is the fact, with verbatim anchors.\n\nFILE: repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/substrate-health-tick.ts\n\nDEFECT, on this exact line (currently 351):\n    : (total_pairs === 0 ? false : pairs_above_floor / total_pairs >= confidenceRatioThreshold);\n\nA bare ratio with a zero-guard but NO MINIMUM-SAMPLE FLOOR, over variant pairs seen in a 3600s window. Measured on the same unchanged system 4h apart: 2/17 = 0.12 FAIL, then 2/4 = 0.50 PASS. THE NUMERATOR NEVER MOVED (2 both times); the denominator collapsed. Degenerate case: 1/1 = a confident PASS on ONE observation. Since CLAUDE.md defines S1->S2 lift as three consecutive coverage_progress=true AND overall_passing=true, an IDLE substrate manufactures lift.\n\nFIX, using the idiom already in this same file. Three lines above:\n    const confidence_passing = !corpus_complete\n      ? null\nand the comment at 345-348 says: 'When the registry corpus could not be fully read, confidence + stability are UNMEASURED (null), never a confident pass/fail. A null dimension makes overall_passing null (\"couldn't measure this tick\"), which resets the lift streak honestly instead of falsely signalling a regression.' A THIN SAMPLE IS OWED THE SAME HONESTY.\n\nAdd a minimum-sample floor that yields null, not false. Follow the existing threshold-read pattern at lines 117-118 (const confidenceFloor = pointer.confidence_floor ?? 10;) by adding const confidenceMinPairs = pointer.confidence_min_pairs ?? 8; and make the predicate return null when total_pairs < confidenceMinPairs. Surface total_pairs and that floor in posterior_confidence so the verdict is legible.\n\nDO NOT lower confidenceRatioThreshold, and DO NOT return false on a thin sample: false reads as a measured regression and asserts the opposite of the truth, which is that the tick could not measure. null is correct and this file already treats it that way.\n\nVERIFY BY CONSEQUENCE: a quiet hour yields overall_passing=null rather than true, and 2 pairs above floor cannot produce a pass at ANY denominator.","kind":"answer","visibility":"public","source":"stateful-ui-vessel"}}
